cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference SignSync, please cite this software."
title: "SignSync: A Real-Time, On-Device ASL-to-Text Recognition Framework for Privacy-Preserving Banking Service Interactions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Almaflehi"
    given-names: "Mohammed Abdulsalam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ALMAFLEHI/SignSync"
url: "https://github.com/ALMAFLEHI/SignSync"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-19"
keywords:
  - "American Sign Language"
  - "accessibility"
  - "on-device machine learning"
  - "TensorFlow Lite"
  - "MediaPipe"
  - "Flutter"
  - "banking communication"
abstract: >-
  SignSync is an academic Flutter and Android prototype that recognizes 40
  isolated American Sign Language banking intents on-device, guides the user
  through confirmation and request selection, and presents a banker-readable
  request without uploading camera frames or relying on cloud inference.
